       if event.is_action_pressed("run"):
           SPEED *= 1.5
       elif event.is_action_released("run"):
           SPEED /= 1.5

       if event.is_action_pressed("movement_up"):
           movement_direction += -camera.global_transform.basis.y
       elif event.is_action_released("movement_up"):
           movement_direction -= -camera.global_transform.basis.y
       if event.is_action_pressed("movement_right"):
           movement_direction += camera.global_transform.basis.x
       elif event.is_action_released("movement_right"):
           movement_direction -= camera.global_transform.basis.x
       if event.is_action_pressed("movement_down"):
           movement_direction += camera.global_transform.basis.y
       elif event.is_action_released("movement_down"):
           movement_direction -= camera.global_transform.basis.y       
       if event.is_action_pressed("movement_left"):
           movement_direction += -camera.global_transform.basis.x
       elif event.is_action_released("movement_left"):
           movement_direction -= -camera.global_transform.basis.x       

       var mouse_position = get_viewport().get_mouse_position()
       var mouse_direction_projected = camera.project_ray_normal(mouse_position) 
       # Convert screen mouse position to world space direction.
       mouse_direction = Vector3(mouse_direction_projected.z, -1.0 * mouse_direction_projected.x, -1.0 * mouse_direction_projected.y)
   ```

   In the `process` function, multiply the world direction vectors with input movements and apply them as linear and angular velocities to the player's movement:

   ```
   func _process(delta):
       if keyboard.is_action_pressed("movement_forward"):
           movement_direction *= SPEED
       if keyboard.is_action_pressed("movement_backward"):
           movement_direction *= -SPEED
